index 0775a2f..9320919 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ All notable codex-tui changes are recorded here.
 
 ### Audit hardening
 
+- Unify RPC admission and wire quarantine for truthful bootstrap/headless connectivity, skip optional probes on unusable sessions, and preserve the first Registry diagnostic. Add actual-binary count/byte overload and Registry-fault cases plus a healthy optional-method rejection control.
+
 - Quarantine cancelled/failed outbound frames and broken read/decode/EOF transports; bound every write, preserve healthy RPC rejections/response-wait cancellation, and report disconnected headless probes truthfully. Add deterministic partial-write/flush regressions, local wire fault tests and two packaged-binary probe cases.
 
 - Preserve bounded stdio framing across cancellation and deliver the final closed-channel disconnect snapshot exactly once; retain timeout and fail-closed transport behavior.
diff --git a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
index d6cc0e9..6835b13 100644
--- a/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
+++ b/docs/guides/troubleshooting.md
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ RPC notifications retain at most 1024 messages and 16 MiB of accounted payload.
 
 A cancelled or failed outbound write quarantines the connection: partial delivery is unknown, so later requests cannot append to an unfinished frame and writes are never automatically replayed. Every outbound write also has a five-second deadline, including notifications. Wire read/decode failure or EOF during an RPC cannot be misreported as a healthy connection. A valid optional-method RPC rejection and cancellation while merely waiting for a response do not poison an otherwise intact wire.
 
+Connection status covers the entire RPC session, not just its wire: either a retained-message admission failure or a transport failure makes it unusable and disconnected. A quarantined Registry bootstrap skips optional loaded-list probes and preserves the original fault. A valid optional-method rejection still reports a connected but degraded session.
+
